  "testament": "new",
  "chapter": 6,
  "sortOrder": 49006,
  "verseCount": 24,
  "aliases": [
    "Eph",
    "Ephes"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Children, obey your parents in the Lord: for this is right.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Honour thy father and mother; which is the first commandment with promise;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "That it may be well with thee, and thou mayest live long on the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "And, ye fathers, provoke not your children to wrath: but bring them up in the nurture and admonition of the Lord.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Servants, be obedient to them that are your masters according to the flesh, with fear and trembling, in singleness of your heart, as unto Christ;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Not with eyeservice, as menpleasers; but as the servants of Christ, doing the will of God from the heart;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "With good will doing service, as to the Lord, and not to men:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Knowing that whatsoever good thing any man doeth, the same shall he receive of the Lord, whether he be bond or free.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "And, ye masters, do the same things unto them, forbearing threatening: knowing that your Master also is in heaven; neither is there respect of persons with him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Finally, my brethren, be strong in the Lord, and in the power of his might.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Put on the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to stand against the wiles of the devil.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "For we wrestle not against flesh and blood, but against principalities, against powers, against the rulers of the darkness of this world, against spiritual wickedness in high places.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Wherefore take unto you the whole armour of God, that ye may be able to withstand in the evil day, and having done all, to stand.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Stand therefore, having your loins girt about with truth, and having on the breastplate of righteousness;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "And your feet shod with the preparation of the gospel of peace;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Above all, taking the shield of faith, wherewith ye shall be able to quench all the fiery darts of the wicked.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And take the helmet of salvation, and the sword of the Spirit, which is the word of God:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Praying always with all prayer and supplication in the Spirit, and watching thereunto with all perseverance and supplication for all saints;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "And for me, that utterance may be given unto me, that I may open my mouth boldly, to make known the mystery of the gospel,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "For which I am an ambassador in bonds: that therein I may speak boldly, as I ought to speak.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "But that ye also may know my affairs, and how I do, Tychicus, a beloved brother and faithful minister in the Lord, shall make known to you all things:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Whom I have sent unto you for the same purpose, that ye might know our affairs, and that he might comfort your hearts.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Peace be to the brethren, and love with faith, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:ephesians:6:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Grace be with all them that love our Lord Jesus Christ in sincerity. Amen.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ephesians 6:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ephesians:6:24"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
